  "justifications": {
    "limitations": "R2.2 e78cb9f2 measured 12677 B against 11121 B at the B-integration measure (+1556 B) and 11056 B on the R2.1 panel. All growth is four existing limitation entries that now state the sleeve basis of p123-ai-factor, no entry is added and none is duplicated: flow timing bounds +527 B (the parent-account series its row is restated from), HWM member series +330 B (the sleeve series start and the days it carries no value), product perimeter +303 B (sleeve gains and entry-day differences), sleeve capital basis +461 B (gross allocations and margin-funded allocations). These disclose what changed under the restatement; trimming was declined. Limit = measured + 1%, rounded up to 1000 B by tools/panel_payload_size.py --raise-block limitations.",
    "strategies": "R2 committed 121117 B, R2.1 131808 B (+10691 B), R2.1 re-measure 159372 B with the levered/unlevered columns. R2.2 (AI Factor restated to the sleeve basis, #624) measured 176386 B on d7d26c09 and +509 B more with the basis statements (parent-account tags on execution_cost, its EXECUTION component, the live-series summary and the provider overlap, and the execution cost in the not-restated label): 176895 B against 159372 B (+17523 B, +11.0%). Measured field by field against the pre-restatement 4dcb46c1 panel (137237 B), the growth sits in the rows the restatement changes: p123-ai-factor +25884 B (implementation_return_attribution +12545, implementation_reconciliation +5321, comparison_basis +2333, provider_account_basis +1722, benchmark_account_basis +1678, return_levered_* and return_unlevered_* columns about +1700, sleeve_return_windows +283, declared +450), tt-portfolio +4570 B and grizzlybears-vtma +4816 B (implementation_reconciliation and implementation_return_attribution now keep the account-basis legs), volatis-strategy +3573 B (fee_rates +2621, cost_rate_disclosure +763), and 22 B of return_levered_na_reason and return_unlevered_na_reason on each of the other rows. No row is duplicated and no per-observation series is added; the sleeve bridge is the primary row and the account legs sit under account_basis, which is the disclosure the restatement exists to make. Trimming was declined. Limit = measured + 1%, rounded up to 1000 B by tools/panel_payload_size.py --raise-block strategies; the measure is the d7d26c09 figure plus the +509 B simulated on the seat packet (the generation itself was retired), to be confirmed on the final build.",
    "performance": "New top-level block (distinct from performance_tab) carried since R2: 54048 B on R2 b216a53e, 54055 B on R2.1. It was unlisted and sat 4 KB over the 50000 B unlisted-block threshold, so the checker flagged it on every generation. Within 7 B between R2 and R2.1. Limit = committed + 3%, rounded up to 1000 B.",
    "performance_tab": "R2.1 re-measure 381004 B (schema 3: union grid, flow-matched benchmarks), against 375785 B on the r21-integration panel the previous limit was cut from. The limit is re-cut at committed + 3% (393000 B, was 388000 B at 98.2% of committed) so the block has the same headroom every other block has.",
    "weekly_returns": "R2.1 re-measure 27773144 B against 27317555 B at R2 (+1.7%). Per-observation series are the block this budget exists to watch, so the limit is re-cut at committed + 3% (28607000 B, was 28138000 B at 97.4% of committed); further growth needs its own reason.",
    "strategy_underwriting": "R2.2 d7d26c09 measured 73615 B against 64495 B committed (+9120 B, +14.1%). The block holds seven rows and the growth is one layer: evidence_layers.implementation_reconciliation, which mirrors the strategy's implementation_reconciliation row and now carries the account-basis legs for the strategies whose implementation is bridged (grizzlybears-vtma 3054 to 7742 B, tt-portfolio 5849 to 10279 B on the 4dcb46c1 panel), while p123-ai-factor's layer is the sleeve bridge and falls from 14250 to 560 B. The mirror of the strategies row is existing design, not new duplication; trimming was declined because the layer is the disclosure the underwriting row stands on. The basis statements of R2.2 do not change this block. Limit = measured + 1%, rounded up to 1000 B by tools/panel_payload_size.py --raise-block strategy_underwriting.",
    "model_vs_actual": "R2.2 bae512c5 measured 138438 B and +1587 B more with the final-seat basis statements: the p123-ai-factor windows and epochs (10 rows, each +basis and basis_label, about 150 B) and its portfolio-bridge line now say they are the parent account's figures (the audit input measures the whole parent account, not the restated sleeve): 140025 B. No window, epoch or component is added or duplicated; the sleeve comparison stays in governed_reference. Trimming was declined because the label is the statement the owner's basis ruling requires. Limit = measured + 1%, rounded up to 1000 B by tools/panel_payload_size.py --raise-block model_vs_actual; to be confirmed on the final build."
  },
